{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2330 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "01f3ce44e64e6076fccdb7d92059bb3a51c8f79fac50dc8d26967b23142a6839" :edb/db-before-t 2329 :edb/db-after-t 2330 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535642 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:20:43.747Z" 13194139535642 true] [17592186124356 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358999 13194139535642 true] [17592186124356 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359006 13194139535642 true] [17592186124356 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359020 13194139535642 true] [17592186124357 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359013 13194139535642 true] [17592186124357 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359027 13194139535642 true] [17592186358999 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359000 13194139535642 true] [17592186358999 1089 "q-132585" 13194139535642 true] [17592186358999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535642 true] [17592186358999 1100 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=-2.$ Given that the point $P(4,-2,5)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y\\sqrt{x}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186358999 1113 #uuid "25f6db5c-5ba1-51f0-8059-274ba50d3f64" 13194139535642 true] [17592186358999 1145 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(4,-2,5)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(4,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)} & =(-2)\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =-2(2) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(4,-2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)}(x-4) \\\\ z-5 & =-4(x-4) \\\\ z & =-4x+21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(4,-2,5)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+21\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359001 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359002 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359003 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359004 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359005 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1041 "selection" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359001 13194139535642 true] [17592186359000 1110 #uuid "bee217ad-b2d9-5169-98b0-c475e414c6ae" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359001 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+21\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359001 1111 #uuid "6733e913-504e-5778-8c06-ca47d4373929" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359002 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-2x+15\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359002 1111 #uuid "4d0665e3-460a-5613-89ab-f2af8f9e7b72" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359003 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+9\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359003 1111 #uuid "cc7f8de1-4641-5d8b-b25c-5793b8a73f8b" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359004 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=2x+9\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359004 1111 #uuid "2303b7a0-e6f0-5da2-8c5b-dc52f9f676e3" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359005 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=2x+21\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359005 1111 #uuid "c2311db1-071e-5ef9-8c11-f7899b0d9ebd" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359006 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359007 13194139535642 true] [17592186359006 1089 "q-132593" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359006 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535642 true] [17592186359006 1100 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359006 1113 #uuid "f33b32cc-e271-575d-84a5-5374b57e2868" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359006 1145 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi /4)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,\\pi /4)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi /4)}(y-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ z-0 & =4(y-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ z & =4y-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359008 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359009 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359010 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359011 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359012 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1041 "selection" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359010 13194139535642 true] [17592186359007 1110 #uuid "7cb05a8e-bcc1-5318-aa7b-7ad59500d31f" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359008 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=2y+\\pi \\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359008 1111 #uuid "4fbfea36-5d29-5aee-b660-f9a7c359d2d6" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359009 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=2y-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359009 1111 #uuid "18e40470-6d72-53b5-a86a-938e6ef8f4ad" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359010 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-\\pi \\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359010 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359010 1111 #uuid "79f9cc3e-345f-5c24-b1a0-3b48b5f6fddb" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359011 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359011 1111 #uuid "c41e9a55-6bf1-5031-90a2-6b4ad9e2aa6d" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359012 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359012 1111 #uuid "77259452-352b-502d-afd5-e763cd888585" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359014 13194139535642 true] [17592186359013 1089 "q-132604" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535642 true] [17592186359013 1100 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P(1,0,-1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=x{e}^{xy}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359013 1113 #uuid "67f0915e-8edd-59e2-80b4-1117b541be88" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359013 1145 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(1,0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(1,0) & ={f}_{y}(1,0)(y-0) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(-1)y \\\\ z & =-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,0,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=-y-1$ (or $y+z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $-j+k.$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359015 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359016 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359017 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359018 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359019 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1041 "selection" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359015 13194139535642 true] [17592186359014 1110 #uuid "8def2af8-3391-58ae-89cc-ebecfc3d6c0a" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359015 1034 "-j+k" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359015 1111 #uuid "84c0fad5-1808-54fd-a155-1192b4f21e9f" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359016 1034 "-j+2\\,k" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359016 1111 #uuid "99322434-3d73-5ed8-b308-b3368809bda5" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359017 1034 "-2\\,j+k" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359017 1111 #uuid "a141253e-808d-5329-9f37-b3337a4dac30" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359018 1034 "2j-3k" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359018 1111 #uuid "825cdb80-67cc-5ec8-a729-db04bbe0c8e0" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359019 1034 "j+k" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359019 1111 #uuid "2062157a-ebd1-5991-b6ad-331e706b1976" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359020 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359021 13194139535642 true] [17592186359020 1089 "q-71209" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359020 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535642 true] [17592186359020 1100 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,2,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}={x}^{2}y+2x-y$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359020 1113 #uuid "5ac15352-1fbf-549f-af42-188c0083e8a4" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359020 1145 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(-2,2,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(-2,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-1 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359022 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359023 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359024 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359025 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359026 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1041 "selection" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359024 13194139535642 true] [17592186359021 1110 #uuid "f9e8ca98-bb38-506c-8b43-32cc7b1fb8f4" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359022 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-5\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359022 1111 #uuid "3bae643e-1bdc-571d-8105-14b6d1ce452a" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359023 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y-5\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359023 1111 #uuid "34cb866c-8fd8-5e81-a193-16af194c6d6f" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359024 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-3\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359024 1111 #uuid "958b90a8-8432-5cde-bc5e-b3fbfe24ec0e" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359025 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y-3\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359025 1111 #uuid "40768e28-22e9-5d4d-b1c9-3f1dd77a9b27" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359026 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=6y-3\\end{aligned}" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359026 1111 #uuid "5d5ba7d4-7ac0-5ba1-8b74-d7d276bde3b9" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359027 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359028 13194139535642 true] [17592186359027 1089 "q-71234" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359027 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535642 true] [17592186359027 1100 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-1.$ Given that the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\frac{x(y-x)}{2x(y+1)}$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359027 1113 #uuid "7e47a1d1-b7ad-556f-b8e2-ccf1072e819b" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359027 1145 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-1,0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-1,0) & =\\frac{(-1)(0-(-1))}{2(-1)(0+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-1,0) & ={f}_{y}(-1,0)(y-0) \\\\ z-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}y \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-1,0,\\frac{1}{2})$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1 \\\\ z=\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}$ (or $y-2z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2\\,j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,2,1⟩.$" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359029 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359030 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359031 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359032 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359033 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1041 "selection" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359032 13194139535642 true] [17592186359028 1110 #uuid "326dc4d2-50e3-5873-b080-f56fff5c5e6c" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359029 1034 "⟨0,0,1⟩" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359029 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359029 1111 #uuid "8bf5a94b-3053-5a2d-9be2-e8941d23fa72" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359030 1034 "⟨0,-2,1⟩" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359030 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359030 1111 #uuid "486d9ebb-2f5f-59ee-aac1-feb69066749a" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359031 1034 "⟨0,1,1⟩" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359031 1111 #uuid "b84f05f1-2f47-5379-ab0c-8f290e0b0f70" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359032 1034 "⟨0,2,1⟩" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359032 1111 #uuid "d1771ec2-806f-56e1-8fc2-f90eb286008a" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359033 1034 "⟨0,1,-2⟩" 13194139535642 true] [17592186359033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535642 true] [17592186359033 1111 #uuid "1a8ed7fe-a12e-594f-a108-0929ce3c6797" 13194139535642 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-132585" 17592186358999 "q-132585/selection" 17592186359000 "q-132585/selection/10f07a243b6232ea507f28b7dc2604b7d622b7f7d88d8b733246fa33a2ae8c5a" 17592186359001 "q-132585/selection/6a2248e6f4491d7909b2e33d06c08ce9f16dbb12c7cc1ba746430f25c418ec76" 17592186359002 "q-13